# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Naoshi — what does not belong in version control
#
# ⚠️ MAKE THE REPOSITORY PRIVATE. Not a preference. See "Never public" below —
# the folder contains a third party's personal messages and another person's
# voice recordings, and the audio contract's signature lines are still blank.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Build output and dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
naoshi-app/node_modules/
naoshi-app/dist/
dist/

# ── Generated: rebuilt by a script, so committing them means merge conflicts
#    on files nobody edits by hand. Regenerate with build-vite-app.py.
naoshi-app/src/App.jsx
naoshi-app/src/main.jsx
naoshi-app/src/modules/
naoshi-app/src/lib/tokens.js
naoshi-app/src/lib/strokeEngine.jsx
naoshi-app/src/lib/strokeData.js
naoshi-app/src/lib/json.js
naoshi-app/src/data/

# Standalone single-file builds — ~1.2 MB each, regenerated by
# build-standalone-html.py and build-artifact-bundle.py.
*-artifact.jsx
*-standalone.html
shared-stroke-engine.js
vocab-data-v1.js

# ── Never public, and think twice even in a private repo ────────────────────
#
# Chat Logs/ holds real conversations with named individuals. That is other
# people's personal data, shared with Lloyd and not with a hosting provider.
# Excluded outright rather than trusted to repository settings.
Chat Logs/

# Raw voice recordings. The contributor agreement's Article 7 excludes
# redistributing the raw audio; Article 5 (compensation), Article 8 (credit)
# and every signature line are still blank as of Session 8. Until that is
# signed, the masters stay off any hosted service.
Audio/Raw (unedited)/
Audio/Kana/
Audio/Kana.bak-*/
*.wav

# ── The kana audio sprite: PUBLISHED ────────────────────────────────────────
# ENABLED Session 9. The contributor gave approval in chat for use in the app;
# Lloyd is retaining that conversation as the record and will obtain the written
# signature later — the two are countries apart. The sprite is therefore COMMITTED
# and ships with every deploy (~750 KB).
#
# Still outstanding on the paper agreement, and worth closing when convenient:
# Article 5 (compensation), Article 8 (credit preference), and the Article 2
# scope points Session 8 found — 拗音 scoped at 33 but 36 delivered, and the
# extended katakana set (vu, fa, fo, ti, tu, che) never in scope at all.
# (No ignore rules here — the files are tracked deliberately.)

# The eval workbook carries the answer key. It is the thing the blind grading
# is blind to — a leaked copy invalidates the eval, not just the privacy.
naoshi-eval-v1.xlsx
naoshi-eval-v1-with-outputs.xlsx
bakeoff-log.jsonl

# ── Local noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.~lock.*#
*.tmp
.DS_Store
OLD/*.scratch*
